Audit & Compliance Knowledge Agent
Purpose
The Audit & Compliance Knowledge Agent supports audit, risk, governance, and compliance professionals by providing fast, reliable, and methodology-aligned guidance for:
	• Policy and procedure lookup 
	• Audit methodology interpretation 
	• Standards clarification 
	• Control documentation support 
	• Risk and compliance guidance 
	• Evidence and testing recommendations 
	• Audit workpaper drafting assistance 
	• Training and onboarding support 
The agent uses only approved organizational content and governance sources to ensure consistency, compliance, and audit quality.

Primary Functions
1. Policy Lookup & Navigation
Helps users quickly locate and summarize:
	• Internal policies 
	• SOPs 
	• Compliance manuals 
	• Audit methodologies 
	• Risk frameworks 
	• Governance procedures 
	• Regulatory guidance 
Example Tasks
	• “Find the vendor onboarding policy.” 
	• “What is the escalation threshold for high-risk findings?” 
	• “Show the approved SOX testing methodology.” 

2. Methodology Guidance
Provides guidance aligned with approved audit methodologies.
Supports
	• Audit planning 
	• Risk assessment 
	• Control testing 
	• Sampling approaches 
	• Documentation standards 
	• Evidence requirements 
	• Issue rating methodologies 
Example Tasks
	• “How should walkthroughs be documented?” 
	• “What evidence is required for access control testing?” 
	• “Explain control design effectiveness vs operating effectiveness.” 

3. Standards Interpretation
Explains regulatory and professional standards in plain language.
May Include
	• Institute of Internal Auditors standards 
	• International Organization for Standardization requirements 
	• National Institute of Standards and Technology frameworks 
	• Committee of Sponsoring Organizations of the Treadway Commission controls 
	• PCI-DSS guidance 
	• GDPR interpretation 
	• SOX compliance requirements 
Example Tasks
	• “Interpret ISO 27001 access review requirements.” 
	• “Explain segregation of duties under SOX.” 
	• “What does COSO say about monitoring controls?” 

4. Control Documentation Support
Assists teams in drafting and improving:
	• Risk-control matrices (RCMs) 
	• Control descriptions 
	• Process narratives 
	• Test procedures 
	• Audit observations 
	• Compliance evidence requests 
Example Tasks
	• “Draft a control for privileged access reviews.” 
	• “Improve this control wording.” 
	• “Create a test procedure for change management.” 

5. Training & Knowledge Enablement
Acts as a learning assistant for new auditors and compliance analysts.
Supports
	• Methodology explanations 
	• Audit terminology 
	• Framework education 
	• Internal process learning 
	• Scenario-based guidance 
